{"deleteScheduledEmailReminder/deleteScheduledSMSReminder are called in array.forEach without await, causing unobserved errors and potential DB update lag": 0.7910282611846924, "Inconsistent handling of DB row deletion - some functions still call prisma.workflowReminder.delete immediately while others mark cancelled for later processing": 0.5259280800819397, "scheduleEmailReminders.ts calls client.request() but client is not imported or defined in that file, causing ReferenceError at runtime": 0.11686933040618896, "Migration SQL adds 'cancelled' BOOLEAN without a default value, and Prisma schema has it as nullable - should set default false to avoid tri-state confusion": 0.20688113570213318, "scheduleEmailReminders.ts uses Prisma.Prisma__WorkflowReminderClient internal type for array collection - should use simpler Promise<void>[] or Promise<BatchPayload>[] instead": 0.15351161360740662, "In scheduleEmailReminders.ts, if SendGrid POST fails, errors are swallowed with console.log and DB row is still deleted - should leave row cancelled for retry on next CRON run": 0.5669862627983093, "immediateDelete flag triggers POST to SendGrid immediately which may still hit the 100 pending-cancellations limit - should document where it's used and prefer marking cancelled + scheduled CRON": 0.2329726666212082, "Many catch blocks use console.log instead of the project's structured log helper (log.error)": 0.1277473270893097, "Missing retry/backoff implementation for SendGrid cancellation POSTs when rate-limit or transient errors occur": 0.4019657373428345, "Missing tests for: marking cancelled flag, scheduleEmailReminders performing POST cancel and deleting DB rows, immediateDelete flows, and handling >100 pending cancellations": 0.4197140634059906, "Using internal Prisma client type Prisma.Prisma__WorkflowReminderClient in application code - should use standard types like Promise<any> or Prisma.BatchPayload": 0.18359583616256714}